-- title:
--   Theorem 2.2 — Exact regularization by random reweighting
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge1$, $S\ge0$, and let $K\subset\mathbb R^d$ be nonempty and compact with $\|\theta\|\le S$ on $K$. For $G\in\mathcal P(K)$ define $f_G(x)=\int_K(2\pi)^{-d/2}e^{-\|x-\theta\|^2/2}\,dG(\theta)$ and $L_n(G)=\sum_i\log f_G(X_i)$. Set $r_n=(\log n/\log\log n)^d$, $\bar r_n=r_n+\log n$, and $\alpha_n=\bar r_n\log n$. For every $b>0$, there are $C>0$ and $n_0$, chosen before the true law $G^*$, such that for every $n\ge n_0$ and $G^*\in\mathcal P(K)$ the following holds. Under iid data $X_i\sim f_{G^*}$ and independent iid weights $W_i\sim\operatorname{Gamma}(\alpha_n,\text{rate }\alpha_n)$, there is a measurable event $E$ with $\mathbb P(E^c)\le Cn^{-b}$. For every $(X,W)\in E$, all weights are positive and $\max_i|W_i-1|\le C/\sqrt{\bar r_n}$. The maximizer set of $\sum_iW_i\log f_G(X_i)$ over all $G\in\mathcal P(K)$ is the singleton $\{\widehat G_W\}$; its topological support is finite and has at most $C\bar r_n$ points. For every ordinary NPMLE $\widehat G_0$, $0\le L_n(\widehat G_0)-L_n(\widehat G_W)\le C/\log n$ and $\sum_i[\log(f_{\widehat G_W}(X_i)/f_{\widehat G_0}(X_i))]^2\le C/\log n$. On the same event, $H^2(f_{\widehat G_W},f_{G^*})\le C(\log n)^{d+1}/[n(\log\log n)^d]$, where $H^2(f,g)=\int_{\mathbb R^d}(\sqrt f-\sqrt g)^2\,dx$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianMainTheorem.lean#L52-L102

